{TEXT("VO_1974_Confess_01"),TEXT("I told myself I had done nothing. That was what I used to say. But I took Elsie there myself. I held her hand all the way to the door.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Confess_02"),TEXT("She asked me if I was coming inside. And I told her to be a good girl. She was. God help me, she was.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_EndA_01"),TEXT("She reached the morning. Exhausted. Unharmed. Her clothes were clean.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_EndA_02"),TEXT("Another child found safe. She struggled to remember. Eventually, the questions stopped.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_EndA_03"),TEXT("First a circle. Then two eyes. Then a smile. Then ten arms.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_EndA_04"),TEXT("Another child found safe.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_EndB_01"),TEXT("Maisie did not want to leave. She said Mim was kind. It never shouted. It never left her alone.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_EndB_02"),TEXT("She called for Mim. Nell hid. Maisie was perfectly calm as the arms gathered her up.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_EndB_03"),TEXT("Maisie Evans. Finished. For a moment, recognition. Perhaps fear. Then she smiled again.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_EndB_04"),TEXT("Eleanor Price. Place prepared. Mim carried Maisie away. Nell remained in the dark.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_01"),TEXT("London. Winter, nineteen seventy-four. The children always disappear one at a time.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_02"),TEXT("Then they come home. Clean. Fed. Polite. They cannot remember where they have been.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_03"),TEXT("Sooner or later, every child draws the same thing. Ten arms. Two great eyes. An impossible smile. They call it Mim.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_04"),TEXT("Eighteen ninety-four. Nineteen thirty-two. Nineteen fifty-eight. Nineteen seventy-three. Different children. The same house. The same careful handwriting.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_05"),TEXT("Maisie Evans remembered. A staircase. A pale face. A great many hands. Her friend Nell believed her.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_06"),TEXT("Nobody else did. Maisie kept a journal. Then she disappeared for the second time.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_07"),TEXT("The second time, I did not want to run. Nell went to the house to find the girl she remembered.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_08"),TEXT("She brought a candle. The entrance closed behind her. Somewhere in the house, something moved.")},
{TEXT("VO_1974_Intro_09"),TEXT("Somewhere safe. That was what Mim called it.")},
