{TEXT("VO_Read_bill_01"),TEXT("MISSING. WILLIAM REES. AGED SEVEN. H Division, Bethnal Green. 1894. Someone kept this notice for eighty years. Underneath, in pencil: found him. he's good now.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_chart_01"),TEXT("TOM 4. TOM 5. TOM 6. TOM 7. His marks stop at seven. Other names begin below them. Dates from different decades. Small soot-black handprints. The higher marks are not a child growing. They are different children standing in the same place.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_drawings_01"),TEXT("A huge bed. A door stretched taller than the wall. A corridor with no end. The drawings are from different decades. The rooms around you look like them. Mim understands a drawing better than it understands a house.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_drawings_02"),TEXT("Ten arms. Two great eyes. An impossible smile. Some children draw Mim holding their hands. Others draw themselves inside its body. They say they do not remember it.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_01"),TEXT("MAISIE EVANS. HER BOOK. KEEP OUT. (that means you Nell) (not really) Winter, 1974. Nell believes me. Nobody else does.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_02"),TEXT("I went into the old house. A staircase. A ceiling too high to see. Then a pale face and all those hands. The first time I ran because I was frightened. I should have run again.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_03"),TEXT("if you woke in the chair, rock with it. push when it tips back. it thinks this is somewhere safe. the candle and matches are on the table. take them. nothing electric in this house gives any light.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_04"),TEXT("IT FOLLOWS THE LIGHT. cup the flame with your hand (right mouse) and it sees less. R puts it out. but then you cant see either. R strikes a match. a match is LOUD.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_05"),TEXT("in the dark it LISTENS. hold your breath (F). stay still. crouching (ctrl) is quieter. running (shift) is loud and can kill the flame. you cant hold your breath forever. if it looks at you, hide. a bed. a wardrobe. somewhere small.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_06"),TEXT("the cellar door has a lock. feel for the pins. hold tension gently. a pin that stays is good. too much and the pick snaps. IT HEARS THE SNAP. more locked rooms upstairs. a way in can become a way out.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_07"),TEXT("there is a crowbar somewhere in the house. use it on the workshop boards. dont pull them all at once if it is close. it hears each one fall. [ I ] is what you carry. [ Q ] puts a tool down. the candle has its own hand.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_08"),TEXT("three fuses. one in the cellar, one in the house, one upstairs. put them in the switchboard. the motor still works. the lamps dont. it releases the attic latch. DONT expect the lights to come on.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_09"),TEXT("the records are older than mum. older than nan. FINISHED doesnt mean safe. the rooms come from our drawings. things are big because thats how we remembered them. it is trying so hard to make a home.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_journal_10"),TEXT("the shelves are upstairs. every candle has a name. if you find mine, look for me. but if I tell you I dont want to go... nell, please remember what I wanted before. M.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_labels_01"),TEXT("Names. Dates. Ages. Not memorials. A record of what was taken. FEAR. HOMESICKNESS. ANGER. REFUSAL. The feelings were preserved in the tallow. When it burns, something of the child escapes.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_labels_02"),TEXT("MAISIE EVANS. FINISHED. Beside her place, an empty mould: ELEANOR PRICE. The light that protected you was made from something stolen.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_letter_01"),TEXT("Dear Elsie, I thought I was keeping you safe. I took your hand and walked you to the house myself. You asked if I was coming inside. I told you to be good. I was there. And I did nothing. Your father.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_maisie_01"),TEXT("The first time I ran because I was frightened. The second time I knew what was there. I should have run again. But I didn't want to anymore.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_maisie_02"),TEXT("nell when you arent afraid of something bad you dont run. when you arent angry you dont fight. being quiet isnt being happy. dont let it finish you. maisie")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_nan_01"),TEXT("Nell love, A little pale light means a child's funeral. A corpse-candle. Never follow it. And don't let anyone tell you there is something wrong with being frightened. Come home. Nan x")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_newspaper_01"),TEXT("EAST LONDON. WINTER 1974. ANOTHER MISSING CHILD RETURNS. The latest disappearance follows incidents recorded in 1894, 1932, 1958 and last winter. Children return clean, fed, and unable to account for their absence. Parents describe remarkable improvements in behaviour.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_newspaper_02"),TEXT("In the margin: Improvement is not the same as recovery. She used to laugh without being asked.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_notebook_01"),TEXT("H Division. Bethnal Green. Eighteen ninety-four. A child described a chair, a pale face and something soft moving above her. The constable wrote: Child's fancy. No further action.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_notebook_02"),TEXT("Many years later, on the next page: I was there. And I did nothing. He had been warned long before Nell was born.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_portrait_01"),TEXT("JOSIAH, RUTH AND THOMAS PRYCE. SPITALFIELDS, 1866. Our Thomas. Such a brave boy. A later note: Aged seven. Trapped in a chimney for two days. His candle went out. He did not survive.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_portrait_02"),TEXT("Josiah blamed the fear. Not the men who sent a child into a chimney. The face of Ruth's unfinished toy was taken from a cast associated with Thomas. Mim is not Josiah. Josiah died. Mim kept working.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_register_01"),TEXT("Pryce. Private register. Thomas Pryce. Aged seven. Died in the flue, eighteen sixty-six. The first entry is crossed out. R. P. \u2014 unsuitable.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_register_02"),TEXT("NAMES. DATES. TREATMENTS. 1894. Alfred Morgan. FINISHED. 1894. Elsie Jenkins. RETURNED. 1932. A new page. A new child. 1958. The same careful hand. 1973. Still the same hand. Josiah could not have written them all.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_register_03"),TEXT("Winter, 1974. MAISIE EVANS. NOT FINISHED. GONE. Underneath, written more slowly: MAISIE EVANS. FINISHED. ELEANOR PRICE. PLACE PREPARED.")},
{TEXT("VO_Read_ruth_01"),TEXT("For our Thomas. You needn't be brave all the time. Love, Mother. Black fabric. Unfinished animals. A needle still in a sleeve. Ruth's name vanishes from the records. The register says only R. P. \u2014 unsuitable.")},
